## Risks, ordering, and assumptions

1. Land the shared union and derived matrix first, with mutation witnesses, before widening behavior.
2. Add root/catch/terminal grammar and entry-role invariants together; otherwise an intermediate tree can emit the wrong connector role.
3. Add public declaration models, immutable map metadata, vetted registry, and shared state analysis before wiring callers.
4. Add the authority resolver, then authoring/recipe/materialization call sites, then revision coverage.
5. Update served text, schemas, projection snapshots, and independently sourced goldens last—but in the same coherent commit.

Key risks:

- A wrong connector-entry role changes emitter selection. Existing index-0 call goldens plus prefixed-call role mutants guard it.
- A matrix test derived from an empty or incomplete key set is vacuous. The terminal and new-context mutants guard both failure modes.
- Passing one capability object to every root produces false unbound-contract errors. Root-local partitioning is mandatory.
- Map metadata can overclaim. Any uncertain family/config is opaque; partial knowledge is never promoted to a complete effect.
- Effect authority changes must rotate compiler/capability revisions. The new revision payload and mutation tests make that structural.
- Apply does not carry trusted effect context in this issue. Compile-time materialization receives it only to build the read-only artifact; existing apply dry materialization remains a pre-write fail-closed boundary.
- The current repository ships no recipe-produced custom script: recipe contribution validation explicitly rejects script, script-body, custom-scripting, and language keys. Therefore the production vetted registry is honestly empty at this HEAD, and the registered-script acceptance case uses an internal server-owned test fixture. Adding a real production seed requires a separately identified server-owned script/recipe and must not be improvised as a digest-only row.
- `AUTHORING_CONTRACT_VERSION`, `PROCESS_IR_VERSION`, and the `process_ir_authoring` contract version remain unchanged; exact schema/capability/compiler hashes record the additive changes.
- The quoted issue probe commit and several quoted line numbers were not re-live-probed in this read-only turn. Current source behavior, current goldens, emitter registrations, and the absence of recipe-shipped scripts were verified at the stated HEAD.
